§ `Date pairs on five signature lines of one issue`

-- DEFECT 4. Kovetz HaTakanot 7639 (24 Adar II 5776, printed 3 April 2016) prints five signature lines of the Minister of Justice with the same pair, "25 Adar I 5776 (8 March 2016)": under the regulations on the first page of the
-- issue's list (p. 946), under two regulations on p. 948, and under a regulation and an order on p. 949. The sources are the official issue only; no consolidation is used.
-- Only the first line, on p. 946, was read from the page image. The other four were read in the text layer of the PDF, whose order of words is garbled; tools/pdfcheck.py confirms that the Hebrew words and the numerals of each typed
-- line occur in the text layer of the page, and nothing about their order.
-- The routine reproduced 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024 first; then 5776 is a leap year, so Adar I is the first of two Adars, and 25 Adar I 5776 = 5 March 2016, 28 Adar I 5776 = 8 March 2016.
-- No right or deadline in this row turns on these lines, and the row shows no effect of the difference.
-- ext:[KT 7639 p.946, read from the page image] | תקנות החברות (הקלות לעניין החובה לקבוע מדיניות תגמול) (תיקון), התשע"ו-2016
-- ext:[KT 7639 p.946, read from the page image] | כ"ה באדר א' התשע"ו (8 במרס 2016)
`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the pair is printed in` IS "Kovetz HaTakanot 7639 printed p. 946, the signature line under the Companies (Relief regarding the Duty to Set a Compensation Policy) (Amendment) Regulations, 5776-2016"
